    ["　　戴莉艰难地笑了笑，对抗着体表不断冒出的白色绒毛和漆黑鳞片道：\n　　“原来是你……\n　　“你之前不是问我，为什么不主动，主动向邓恩表白，将他推到，床上？”\n　　她吸了口气，苦涩笑道：\n　　“我过去有过，太多的放纵，他，他是一个保守的人，我，我很自卑。”\n　　她已快控制不住，即将变成怪物。\n　　这个时候，她听见克莱恩·莫雷蒂回应道：\n　　“队长其实很喜欢你，但你太优秀太年轻了，他也很自卑。”\n　　戴莉笑了，旋即在朦胧的视线里看见了那个身穿黑色风衣，发际线较高，有幽邃灰眸的男人，看见他以手按胸，弯腰伸掌，邀请自己跳舞。\n　　她探出了自己的手，她的思绪随之变得滞涩。\n　　穿黑风衣的灰眸男人拉起了异变逐渐退去的戴莉，在伦纳德的目光中，在喷泉乱流的破败广场里，跳起了轻快的舞蹈。\n　　一样样材料飞出，有金色的葡萄藤，有较为丑陋的橡皮面具，它们在灵性的引导下，逐渐糅合在一起，灌入了一个金属小瓶。\n　　美妙的舞蹈中，戴莉轻轻前靠，倚在了邓恩的怀里。\n\n　　——第四卷《不死者》第二百一十三章 故事的尾声"] = "Daly smiled with difficulty, fighting against the white fluff and pitch-black scales constantly emerging from her skin:\n \"So it was you...\n \"Didn't you ask me before why I didn't take the initiative, take the initiative to confess to Dunn and push him onto the bed?\"\n She took a breath and smiled bitterly:\n \"I've had too much indulgence in the past. He, he is a conservative person, and I, I am very insecure.\"\n She could no longer control herself and was about to turn into a monster.\n At this moment, she heard Klein Moretti respond:\n \"The Captain actually liked you very much, but you were too outstanding and too young, and he was also very insecure.\"\n Daly smiled, and then in her hazy vision, she saw the man in the black trench coat with a high hairline and deep gray eyes. She saw him place his hand on his chest, bow, and extend his palm to invite her to dance.\n She reached out her hand, and her thoughts became stagnant.\n The gray-eyed man in the black trench coat pulled up Daly, whose mutation was gradually receding. Under Leonard's gaze, in the dilapidated square with turbulent fountain water, they danced a light dance.\n Materials flew out one by one—golden grapevines, an ugly rubber mask—and under the guidance of spirituality, they gradually merged together and were poured into a small metal bottle.\n In the midst of the beautiful dance, Daly leaned forward gently and rested in Dunn's arms.\n\n — Volume 4: Undying, Chapter 213: The End of the Story",
    ["　　生活太<Letter_RedBig>辛苦</>了，像我们这样穷苦的人，生来似乎就是为了劳作的。\n　　如果不劳作，今天吃完了饭，就要操心明天的饭在哪里。\n　　如果运气好，工厂给了我劳作的机会，今天工作结束，又要操心明天的工作。\n　　冷的时候，手上会长<Letter_RedBig>疮口</>，一点一点冻掉我的肉。\n　　热的时候，棉絮会钻进我的肺部，让我一点一点咳出我的<Letter_RedBig>灵魂</>。\n　　对我这样的人来说，明天是一种负担。\n　　“永暗的蜡烛，不毁的身躯”，我想要什么也不管，什么也不顾……直接睡过去。"] = "　　Life is too <Letter_RedBig>hard</>. For poor people like us, we seem to be born just to toil.\n　　If we don't toil, once we finish today's meal, we have to worry about where tomorrow's will come from.\n　　If we are lucky and the factory gives me a chance to work, once today's work is done, I have to worry about tomorrow's work.\n　　When it's cold, sores grow on my hands, <Letter_RedBig>sores</> that slowly freeze away my flesh.\n　　When it's hot, cotton fibers drill into my lungs, making me cough out my <Letter_RedBig>soul</> bit by bit.\n　　For someone like me, tomorrow is a burden.\n　　\"Candle of Eternal Darkness, Indestructible Body,\" I want to ignore everything, not care about anything... and just fall asleep.",
